: live flea prices, interactive maps, quest and hideout progression, calculators and an API for Escape from Tarkov, built and run by one person.",intro1:"Tarkov Market is a set of tools for Escape from Tarkov: live flea market prices, interactive maps, quest and hideout progression, profit calculators, a weapon loadout builder and a public API.",intro2:"I started it in 2019 as a plain price checker — I wanted to know what an item was really worth before dragging it out of a raid. It kept growing, and today prices are one section out of many.",intro3:"I design, build and run all of it myself: the website, the scanners behind the prices, the desktop companion app and the API. There is no team here — when something breaks, it is me fixing it.","tools-title":"What is on the site","group-prices":"Prices and market","group-maps":"Interactive maps","group-progress":"Quests and progression","group-calc":"Calculators and gear","group-loadouts":"Weapon loadouts","group-tools":"Apps and integrations","maps-text":"Every map keeps loot, extracts, spawns, keys and quest markers on one canvas. Markers can be filtered, a quest marker links back to the quest it belongs to, and you can draw your own layers and share them. With Tarkov Pilot running, the map follows your position while you play.","data-title":"Where the numbers come from","data-text":"Flea prices come from my own scanners reading the in-game market around the clock, so a price shows the market now, not yesterday's snapshot. Trader prices, crafts, barters and quest data come from the game files after every patch. PVP, PVE and the current season are tracked as separate economies, because their prices have nothing in common.","pro-title":"Free and PRO","pro-text":"Prices, maps, quests and calculators are free. A PRO subscription adds deeper price history, market analytics and higher limits on the parts that cost the most to run. It pays for the servers — the site works without it.","lang-title":"Languages","lang-text":"Th